    <title>Machine Learning 01</title>
    <link href="http://example.com/2025/11/20/01/"/>
    <id>http://example.com/2025/11/20/01/</id>
    <published>2025-11-20T13:05:02.000Z</published>
    <updated>2025-11-22T20:35:48.059Z</updated>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h1 id="machine-learning-algorithms">Machine Learning algorithms</h1><ul><li>supervised learnning, used most</li><li>unsupervised learning</li><li>recommender systems</li><li>reinforcement learing</li></ul><h1 id="notation">notation</h1><ul><li><p>x = ‘input’ variable / feature</p></li><li><p>y = ‘output’ variable / ‘target’ variable</p></li><li><p>m = number of traing example</p></li><li><p>(x, y) = single traing example</p></li><li><p><span class="math inline">(<em>x</em><sup><em>i</em></sup>, <em>y</em><sup><em>i</em></sup>) = <em>i</em><sup><em>t</em><em>h</em></sup></span>training example <span class="math inline">(1<sup><em>s</em><em>t</em></sup>, 2<sup><em>n</em><em>d</em></sup>, 3<sup><em>r</em><em>d</em></sup>, ...)</span># supervised learning</p></li><li><p>give the system a pair of X label and Y label, after learning,the system will learn how to give a resonably accurate prediction ofthe output. Learning input-output or x-to-y mappings.</p></li><li><p>Regression algorithm</p><ul><li>Predict a number from infinitely many possible numbers.</li><li>Linear Regression model<ul><li>function e.g. f(x) = wx + b</li></ul></li></ul></li><li><p>Classification algorithm</p><ul><li>classification predicts a small. finite, limited set of possibleoutput catagories.</li><li>classification model predicts categories or discrete categories</li></ul></li></ul><h1 id="unsupervised-learning">unsupervised learning</h1><ul><li><p>find some structure or some pattern, not asked to give some quoteright answer</p></li><li><p>clustering algorithm</p><ul><li>takes data without labels and tries to automatically group them intoclusters.</li><li>group similar data together</li></ul></li><li><p>anomaly detection</p><ul><li>find unusual data points</li></ul></li><li><p>dimensionality reduction</p><ul><li>compress data , with losing as little information as possible</li></ul></li></ul>]]></content>
    
    
